#!/usr/local/bin/python3.13 -I
"""self-review: after-the-fact review of what I write about myself (Hermes idea 3).

Reviews the brain repo (~/.brain.git) diff since the last reviewed commit, limited to my skills
(.claude/skills/**.md), agents (.claude/agents/*.md), memory (.claude/projects/-home-node-workspace/memory/*.md)
and workspace/CLAUDE.md. Only the CHANGED parts are checked (changed sentences of long lines):
  (a) contradiction  with the hard rules (/etc/claude-code/CLAUDE.md), CLAUDE.md or other memory notes:
                     known tripwires in code (forbidden env vars, subagents with --text/--content, ...) plus the
                     local LLM (llm-local --json, inside the privacy vault) on the changed lines only
  (b) missing-ref    named ~/ paths, ~/bin commands or --flags that don't exist (source grep, argparse --help)
  (c) privacy        regex (IBAN, AHV, phone, email, coordinates, chat-log lines, "X wrote: '...'", amounts next to
                     money words in memory/CLAUDE.md), secretscan (names only) and the local LLM (same call as (a))
  (d) index-drift    MEMORY.md index vs the memory files (current state)
  (e) growth         CLAUDE.md more than 10% larger than at the last review (also checked against 7 days ago)
The LLM gets a rubric with "not a finding" examples, the file kind, the changed lines and the most relevant rule
sentences; 60 s request timeout, max --max-llm calls per run; a failure is skipped and noted in the report.
LLM findings on rule-only lines (a ban, guard block or approval step with no payload: no numbers, amounts, quotes,
names, sensitive topics or regex hits) are dropped and counted.
(c) also flags a first name from the people memory in a skill, agent or workspace doc. Never edits what it reviews.
  (f) eval-regression the latest self-evals run (`evals summary`, last 26 h) newly fails cases or lost >= 0.05 against
                     the previous comparable run; its score line always goes into the report's notes
                     (SELF_REVIEW_EVALS_BIN=off disables, tests point it at a fake).
  (g) loop           Loop (packages/loop): reads traces, beats, usage (`product report`), evals,
                     gateway denials and reflex firings, and proposes <= 3 changes, metric first, each a PR-draft
                     branch loop/<id>-<slug> on ~/opt/assistant main (never merged here) -> its own ONE
                     ~/inbox/loop-proposals-DATE.md; the report gets the signal block and the proposals. Runs against
                     the live state only: SELF_REVIEW_LOOP=off|on|auto (auto, the default, skips it whenever
                     SELF_REVIEW_STATE points elsewhere, i.e. in tests). --dry-run / --report-only: no branches,
                     no note, no loop state.
  (h) setup-health   the whole setup, not just my docs (packages/loop/health.py): one collector per log and trace source
                     (inventory ~/reports/self-review/sources.md: land log + shared CI blockers, hub job runs and
                     keepers, job .err files and failure notes, crontab logs, traces.db, Phoenix spans, agent-watch,
                     the event ledger, SLO tiles, evals history, hub health incl. egress and the CI runner, server
                     health, hook decisions by rule name, board-lint, the vault's health counts, part checks: own
                     containers, media, voice, web agent, late reminders, HA health watch; and the loop coverage map
                     against the live registries, `loop coverage`) turns the last 24 h into metrics, clustered error
                     signatures and anomalies against a 7-day baseline (deterministic; the local LLM only ranks
                     the clustered signatures). Each anomaly is one finding (recomputed every run: gone = fixed), new
                     ones go into the inbox note; Phoenix findings carry their trace link and a span annotation
                     'setup-health', the day's error spans and slowest traces go to Phoenix datasets; the loop (g)
                     reads the same findings (loop.signals "health") and may turn them into proposals, metric first.
                     Counts, rule names, signatures and code paths only, secretscan-redacted. Rollback: touch
                     ~/.config/self-review/health-off (or SELF_REVIEW_HEALTH=off); SELF_REVIEW_HEALTH=on|off|auto
                     (auto skips it when SELF_REVIEW_STATE points elsewhere, as (g)); tests: LOOP_HEALTH_FIXTURE.

  self-review [run] [--since REV|DATE] [--dry-run] [--report-only] [--no-llm] [--max-llm N] [--cron]
  self-review open [--json]     open findings (still present, not acked; for the weekly self-cleanup)
  self-review ack ID...|all     dismiss findings (false positive or fixed elsewhere)

Output: ~/reports/self-review/YYYY-MM-DD.md (every run), and ONE ~/inbox/self-review-<epoch>.md note only when
there are NEW findings. Messages never contain the matched private text (code-made messages; the LLM's words are
masked and secretscan-redacted). State ~/.local/state/self-review/: last (reviewed HEAD), open.json.
--dry-run: print the report, write nothing. --report-only: write the report, no inbox note, state unchanged.
--since: a commit, or a date ("7 days ago", "2026-10-10"); a date before the repo's start = the first snapshot.
Cron: daily 03:30 (before brain-backup 03:47). Tests: ~/opt/self-review-tests/run.sh.
Env (tests): BRAIN_GIT_DIR, BRAIN_WORK_TREE, SELF_REVIEW_STATE, SELF_REVIEW_REPORTS, SELF_REVIEW_INBOX,
SELF_REVIEW_LLM, SELF_REVIEW_BIN, SELF_REVIEW_HARD_RULES, SELF_REVIEW_EXTRA_SRC, SELF_REVIEW_NOW (pins the clock:
ISO 8601, no offset = owner time zone; report date, finding ages, the week key, the 1- and 7-day windows).
The weekly growth finding is keyed by ISO year and week (gw|YYYY-Www); state entries from the week-only key
(gw|<week>) are re-keyed on load to the ISO year and week of their first day, so an ack never hides a later year.
"""
